Z||000006||mrfiero||07-20-2001||11:31 PM||||John,<P>I almost forgot about the VIN's!  I think (don't quote me yet) that this coupe is 1G2PE11R0JP205448.  I'll double check tomorrow (in case my memory isn't so good).  The GT cover was repainted from white to black and I couldn't see a VIN#.  It may not have been from an '88 GT per se......it is the '86-'88 style though.  I'll take a look at it and see if I can find a VIN.<P><BR>fFormula88,<P>This is a U-Pull-It yard that turns over their inventory very quickly.  If a car lasts a week you are lucky (that's why I have to pull off the goodies ASAP.  This is the first '88 Fiero that this yard has ever had......I could have bought the whole thing for $300, but they wanted an additional $10 for each car they had to move to get it out.  Since it was blocked in by 8 cars and since much of the interior was already stripped (and some body panwels missing) it just wasn't worth the $$.  I'll do better in the long run by just buying the parts I need.  I might try to pull off the cradle too.    <P>BTW.....their prices are all generic......they charge the same amount for a given part whether it's from a Cadillac or a Yugo.  <P>I may post in the Mall to see if anyone wants the things I don't need (like Formula/coupe rear fascia, etc.<P>Two88GT's,<P>It's a 5-sp., but the shifter console (along with most of the interior) is gone.  Sorry.<P>  ||||reg||1
